.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_regulation_matrix" "fuzzygene_regulation_matrix"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_regulation_matrix \- Export the signed regulation weight matrix of a trained model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_regulation_matrix(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBlayout\fR as string = "square", 
\fBminWeight\fR as double = 0, 
\fBgenes\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export the signed regulation weight matrix of a trained model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlayout\fB \fR\- \fBsquare\fR (default), \fBregulators\fR or \fBcompact\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminWeight\fB \fR\- edges with a smaller absolute weight are exported as zero; 0 keeps all. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- restrict the exported rows to these target genes; empty means all. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a Matrix object (rows = targets, columns = regulators)
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Rows are target genes, columns are regulators, and the element
 `W[i, j]` is the signed influence of regulator `j` on target `i`
 (the average analytic partial derivative `dx_target/dx_regulator`):
 positive means activation, negative means repression, zero means no modelled edge.
 


 


 The result is a standard \fBMatrix\fR object, so it can be written directly with
 \fBgeneExpression::write.expr_matrix()\fR or fed into downstream network analysis:
 
\fB
 let w = fuzzygene::fuzzygene_regulation_matrix(model, layout = "compact");
 geneExpression::write.expr_matrix(w, file = "/path/to/network_weight.csv", id = "geneID");
 
\fR`

 


 


 Layouts: \fBsquare\fR (strict N x N, rows and columns are all model genes),
 \fBregulators\fR (columns limited to genes that really appear as regulators) and
 \fBcompact\fR (rows = targets with at least one edge, columns = regulators).
 For a genome scale model the square layout is `N^2` doubles
 (about 2.7 GB for 18,533 genes), so prefer \fBcompact\fR/\fBregulators\fR
 together with the \fBgenes\fR row filter.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
